# Cell from playpick: mode=raid, boss=confluence (The Confluence),
# spec=shaman:elemental, style=idle, size=10, difficulty=normal,
# view=390x844,touch, save=fresh.
#
# direction.md #1 has two idle pulls of this exact boss/size/difficulty so
# far: rogue:assassination (melee dps, 2026-09-28-22.play) wiped badly
# (aliveParty=3/10, heroHp=0), and druid:guardian (tank, 2026-09-30-9.play)
# won clean (aliveParty=6/10) because scheduleInfection excludes the tank
# role outright (src/sim/boss.ts:2653, checked by that session). Both idle
# pulls tried so far are either melee-range or immune-by-role; nobody has
# run idle on a *ranged* non-tank spec, so it is still open whether the
# rogue's loss was about the infection/ooze mechanism (which births the ooze
# wherever the carrier is standing and should catch a ranged body just as
# hard as a melee one, since it does not check distance to the boss) or
# about something specific to being in melee range of the boss itself.
# Elemental shaman is a ranged caster, eligible for infection the same as
# the rogue was (non-tank), so this pull should settle that: if it loses the
# same way the rogue did, the mechanism is confirmed geometric-and-role-based
# regardless of range; if it survives like the tank did, range from the boss
# turns out to matter after all.
#
# Reached the documented way: an invite hash unlocks the tier it names and
# everything below it, since a fresh save only opens Bonegrinder 10N.
open #b=confluence&s=10&h=0
tap class:shaman:elemental
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot open

play idle 130
bill
state
shot mid1

play idle 130
bill
state
says
shot end
